    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- The `AUDIT` logger is a `private static final Logger` obtained via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` \u2014 the conventional SLF4J pattern for a named logger, and placing it as a constant at the top of the class is the natural location.\n- The audit emission sits in `createOwner` right after `saveOwner(...)` succeeds, which is exactly where the \"on successful create\" side-effect belongs. No separate unit is warranted for a single log line.\n- It reuses the existing `owner` object's accessors (`getId()`, `getCustomerCode()`, `getRegistrationDate()`) rather than duplicating state, and uses parameterized SLF4J logging.\n- The Javadoc explains the intent concisely without over-engineering, and the controller isn't becoming a catch-all \u2014 this is a small, focused addition to an existing flow.\n\nNo new class or method is needed; adding an audit line to the existing create path is the maintainable choice here.",
